        "original_id": "59f34258-73e5-51d3-afb6-7d4b57c44e25",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: H. G. Wells, Rubén Darío\n- Products: Love and Mr Lewisham\n- Concepts: modernismo\n\nFacts:\n- H. G. Wells was born on 21 September 1866 and died on 13 August 1946.\n- Rubén Darío, born Félix Rubén García Sarmiento, was born on January 18, 1867 and died on February 6, 1916.\n- H. G. Wells was an English writer.\n- Rubén Darío was a Nicaraguan poet who initiated the Spanish-American literary movement known as modernismo.\n- Modernismo flourished at the end of the 19th century.\n- H. G. Wells wrote the 1900 novel Love and Mr Lewisham.\n- Love and Mr Lewisham is subtitled \"The Story of a Very Young Couple\" and is set in the 1880s.",
